{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"previous-quelled-nutria","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe original failure recorded on innovative-dandruffy-deer remains a distinct unresolved symptom: in Gerrit Verified run 31775418405, the authorship fixture merge reported an invalid object for a freshly committed loose blob and git write-tree failed. Direct deletion reproduced the byte-for-byte signature, but the organic deleter was not identified. Gerrit 1769 added object-store forensics for the next occurrence.\n\nThe later Gerrit 1827 failure did not reproduce this class: deleting the implicated blob left both broad and narrow history reads healthy. That later batched-empty / narrow-success recurrence was a separate fixture-contract defect fixed by merged Gerrit 1828. This ticket preserves the unresolved ENOENT work so the repaired recurrence ticket does not falsely claim to solve it.\n\n## Plan\n- On the next organic recurrence, collect the Gerrit 1769 forensic block (fsck, count-objects, object listing with mtimes, and GIT_* environment).\n- Identify and deterministically reproduce the process or environment mechanism that removes or hides a freshly committed reachable loose object.\n- Add a RED regression for the proven mechanism, fix the mechanism class without weakening the fixture topology, and prove GREEN plus exact-defect mutation coverage.\n- Run the repository gates and land through Gerrit before closing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] An organic recurrence supplies the captured object-store forensic block, or an equivalent deterministic local reproduction identifies the deleter.\n- [ ] The deleting or object-hiding mechanism is proven rather than inferred from the invalid-object signature alone.\n- [ ] A behavioral regression is observed RED before the class fix and GREEN afterward.\n- [ ] The exact-defect mutation returns the regression to RED.\n- [ ] Repository lint, typecheck, full tests, Gerrit LLM-Review, and Verified gates pass.","id":"0f8f-8178-96b4-4901","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["test","flaky"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Root-cause unresolved loose-object ENOENT in authorship fixture merge"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786911132290192001,"uuid":"1aad4107-252f-4bca-a273-0c60d64a5410"}